[{"id": "R013", "text": "The person taps the bracket and listens for a tick while acknowledging that the reading continues to change. They suspect they may have left the bracket loose."}, {"id": "R014", "text": "The person tightens the fastener, taps the bracket twice, moves it past the loose fastener, and tightens it again. They tap it twice more and leave it in place."}, {"id": "R015", "text": "The person keeps the fastener beside the bracket, leaves the loose fastener visible, marks the bracket with pencil, and conducts one short test while it remains loose. If the fastener catches, they mark the new position and leave the fastener in place; if readings remain normal, they also leave the fastener in place."}, {"id": "R016", "text": "The person presses the bracket with a thumb, leaves it alone for one short run, tests it against the shaft, and then leaves it beside the rig. If the click remains steady, they mark the loose bracket with grease and leave it beside the rig."}, {"id": "R017", "text": "The person places the bracket on the bench edge, notes that it feels loose, scrapes its edge once, and checks the readings. They hold a finger still, mark the bracket with a thumbnail, and try again."}, {"id": "R018", "text": "The person removes and reinstalls the bracket, removes the loose fastener, and observes that the normal reading continues. They conclude the bracket was wrong and return the loose fastener to its original position."}, {"id": "R019", "text": "The person presses the bracket with a thumb and taps it with a heel, but the loose end slips and then catches on the gear. They watch until the sensor clicks, leave the bracket seated, and test the gear with a folded strip of paper."}, {"id": "R020", "text": "The person turns the bracket between their fingers, notices the loose edge catching, presses it with a thumbnail, and leaves the remaining reading unchanged. The fastener stays in place."}, {"id": "R021", "text": "The person presses the bracket once with a thumbnail and stops, leaving the loose fastener in place. They move it to the back of the rig and keep a small note beside it."}, {"id": "R022", "text": "The person leaves the fastener loose briefly, marks the bracket's position with pencil, moves it once, and applies the same test load. If the bracket still catches, they leave the fastener in place and wait for the next test."}, {"id": "R023", "text": "The person places the fastener on the bench and waits for the loose one to move, then observes the bracket click. They leave the fastener on the bench, check the reading on another piece, and leave the bracket in place."}, {"id": "R024", "text": "The person checks the bracket's edge, states that the loose fastener is not present, and suggests it may be slow. They turn the sensor upside down and inspect the loose fastener."}]
